# std/publish-source (design/agent-publish.md): an ordinary worker
# (design/tool-contract.md). It holds no token: it reads and pushes through its
# neighbour `DEEP-DEPS/github`, the one image the github-token is granted to.
# Nothing is recorded before the push; the lease keeps it safe, and a call
# that does not finish is never run again behind the agent's back.
HELP=<<END
Publish the exact commit of the source tree `root` names (such as sources/repo/01-layer) to an HTTPS Git repository branch, preserving its history. Test and inspect the intended PR diff first. Resolve merge conflicts and clear .caos/conflicts before publishing. The server rejects files matched by the source commit's .gitignore rules, including tracked files, and lists them; remove them, adjust the rules, or set allow-ignored. It never strips files or rewrites commits. This does not create a PR (caos-std/github opens one) or change the source tree. Without force the update must be a create or a fast-forward, leased on the branch's head as read when the call runs. With force (replacing the branch's history, as when publishing a squashed stack layer), pass expected: the head you looked at, read with caos-std/github's `head` op, or `absent` for a new branch; the push moves the branch only from exactly that commit, so a change you have not seen is never overwritten. A conflict means the branch moved: import and merge it, then publish again. On an uncertain result, read the branch before acting again.
@param repository HTTPS Git repository URL, without credentials.
@param branch Destination branch name (without refs/heads/).
@param [force] true to allow a non-fast-forward update (a force push); needs expected.
@param [expected] With force: the branch's head as you saw it, a full commit hash, or `absent`.
@param [allow-ignored] true to publish even though tracked files match the commit's .gitignore rules.
@root
@request-id
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --github:@=DEEP-DEPS/github --help=$HELP
